      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, the way we perform this operation in GCA, and the way MediaStore is designed for is to insert a pending entry in mediaStore, write the data, publish it by setting the IS_PENDING bit to 0.\n\nSo in this case, the contentvalues you use to insert the item should set IS_PENDING to 1 in the beginning. And then use the Uri to write the bitmap, and after that publish the item with a \n```\nContentValues publishValues \u003d new ContentValues();\npublishValues.put(Media.IS_PENDING, 0);\nresover.update(uri, publishValues);\n```\nIn case of an exception, in the catch clause you can delete the uri if it\u0027s not null.\n\nYou can look at open and publish methods in https://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/java/com/google/android/libraries/camera/storage/fs/PendingFileObject.java for reference",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 180,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 180,
        "endChar": 13
      },
